{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.three_not_gammaGamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.three_not_gammaGamma","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L281-L287","doc":"**The quark block's length is odd**, so it is not γγ-produced either. Stated\nfor a general three-letter word since the census's quark block is three typed\ncrossings whose generators are not fixed by the corpus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.gluonPair_not_gammaGamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.gluonPair_not_gammaGamma","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L274-L279","doc":"**The gluon pair is not γγ-produced** — both its letters are positive, and\na vertex pairs a positive crossing with a negative one. So the ruling does not\nreach the gluon letters even though their block has even length. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.gluonPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.gluonPair","kind":"def","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L271-L272","doc":"The two-letter gluon block `σ₀σ₀` of the census word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.eleven_not_gammaGamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.eleven_not_gammaGamma","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L260-L269","doc":"**No 11-crossing word is γγ-produced.**\n\n`qou-1qsw` fixes the nucleon crossing budget at 11, which is odd. So the γγ\nruling cannot determine a nucleon word in full — for *any* candidate at that\nbudget, in any order. This bounds the principle's reach from above without\ncomputing anything. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.not_gammaGamma_of_odd_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.not_gammaGamma_of_odd_length","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L255-L258","doc":"**Odd length excludes γγ production.** The contrapositive, in the form the\ncrossing-budget argument uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.gammaGamma_length_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.gammaGamma_length_even","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L245-L253","doc":"**A γγ-word has even length.** Each pair-production vertex contributes\nexactly two letters, so the length of any concatenation of them is even. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.cores_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.cores_ne","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L206-L212","doc":"**The two cores are different elements, not merely different spellings** —\nrecorded so a reader does not assume the orderings are interchangeable. They\nshare a letter multiset; `H₃(q)` is noncommutative across generators, and the\nmeasured traces differ by a factor of 5.5 (`0.9986` against `0.1801` at the\nproton `q₀`). The Lean statement is the weaker, decidable one: the two words\nare not equal as lists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.not_gammaGamma_genGroupedCore","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.not_gammaGamma_genGroupedCore","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L198-L204","doc":"**The gen-grouped core is NOT γγ-produced**, so the ruling excludes it.\n\nTogether with `interleavedCore_isGammaGamma` this settles the ordering: of the\ncensus's two models, exactly one has a γγ-produced core. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.interleavedCore_isGammaGamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.interleavedCore_isGammaGamma","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L193-L196","doc":"**The interleaved core IS γγ-produced.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.genGroupedCore","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.genGroupedCore","kind":"def","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L189-L191","doc":"The gen-grouped core — the **same six letters**, all `σ₀` first. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.interleavedCore","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.interleavedCore","kind":"def","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L185-L187","doc":"The interleaved confinement core `(σ₀σ₁⁻¹)³`, as the census's `nuc9` builds\nit: three pair-production vertices on strands `(0,1,2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.not_gammaGamma_of_snd_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.not_gammaGamma_of_snd_pos","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L171-L183","doc":"**A word whose SECOND crossing is positive is not γγ-produced.**\n\nThis is the lemma that rules out the gen-grouped ordering. It was first stated\nwith both of the first two letters positive as hypotheses; the linter caught\nthat the first is never used, so the lemma is strictly stronger than the\nexclusion needs — the sign of `c₀` is irrelevant. A γγ-word's letters come in\n`(positive, negative)` pairs, so *any* positive letter in second position is\nalready impossible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.gammaGamma_snd_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.gammaGamma_snd_neg","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L162-L169","doc":"**The second letter of a γγ-word is a negative crossing.**\n\nImmediate from the constructor — `vertex i` is `⟨i, true⟩ :: ⟨i+1, false⟩ :: _`\n— but it is the whole content of the ordering exclusion below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.borromean_is_covered","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.borromean_is_covered","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L127-L132","doc":"**The Borromean core is γγ-produced**, so it is one of the words this prune\ncovers — recorded because it is the word `GammaGammaSelectorH3` selects as the\nminimal non-zero survivor, and therefore the one a reader would reach for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.scaled_oneDim_annihilates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.scaled_oneDim_annihilates","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L113-L125","doc":"**The level-1 statement, in the form the decay ansatz uses.**\n\nAt Wenzl level 1 the Markov trace is supported on the `(3)` block alone, so the\nfunctional is `c · χ_(3)` for a scalar `c`. On a γγ-selected `Δ` that is `c · 0`.\nStated for a general scalar and a general unit-on-vertices character so it\napplies to whichever one-dimensional block carries the support. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.altChar_difference_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.altChar_difference_vanishes","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L106-L111","doc":"**Instantiation: the alternating block cannot see a γγ difference.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.altChar_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.altChar_nil","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L102-L104","doc":"The `(1³)` alternating character satisfies the hypotheses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.oneDim_annihilates_gammaGamma_difference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.oneDim_annihilates_gammaGamma_difference","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L89-L100","doc":"**Hence it annihilates every difference of two γγ-produced words.**\n\nThis is the prune: a functional supported on the one-dimensional blocks cannot\nsee *any* γγ-selected `Δ`, whatever the two words are. No scan over candidate\nwords can change the answer, because the answer does not depend on them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.unit_on_vertices_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.GammaGammaDelta.unit_on_vertices_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/GammaGammaSelectedDeltaVanishes.lean#L75-L87","doc":"**A unit-on-vertices multiplicative functional is `1` on every γγ-word.**\n\nThe three hypotheses are exactly the structure both one-dimensional characters\nof `H₃` have: a value on the empty word, multiplicativity over concatenation,\nand the value `1` on a pair-production vertex (the vertex pairs `σᵢ` with\n`σᵢ₊₁⁻¹`, so the two eigenvalues cancel). ","signatureChunk":0}]}